5273:<a id="turn-hook-not-loaded"></a>
5274-
5275-`turn_hook_not_loaded`: the per-turn hook that puts "check GBrain first"
5276-beside every user turn is not running in the harness. Agents use the brain
5277-when that rule reaches them on every turn; the MCP tool list or an
5278-instruction file alone rarely gets the brain used. The `reason` says what
5279-the install check found:
5280-
5281-- `missing`: no gbrain per-turn hook is configured for the harness.
5282-- `untrusted`: the hook is configured but the harness will not run it yet
5283-  (Codex: no matching trust entry, trust it in `/hooks`; OpenClaw:
5284-  `hooks.allowConversationAccess` is off; Hermes: the command is not in
5285-  `shell-hooks-allowlist.json`).
5286-- `hook_failed`: the Claude Code or Codex hook command exited non-zero.
5287-- `no_rule`: the hook ran but added no rule, usually because the
5288-  brain-first block for that harness was opted out.
5289-- `not_loaded`: the harness's own check does not show the hook loaded.
5290-
5291-Run `fix.argv` (it re-runs the install that writes the hook), then check
5292-with the harness's own command:
5293-
5294-| Harness | Check |
5295-|---|---|
5296-| Claude Code | `/hooks` in a session lists the UserPromptSubmit hook |
5297-| Codex | `/hooks` in a session; trust the hook there if it asks |
5298-| OpenClaw | `openclaw plugins inspect gbrain-turn-rule --runtime --json` shows it loaded with `before_prompt_build` |
5299-| Hermes | `hermes hooks doctor` shows the `pre_llm_call` hook healthy |
5300-
5301-`gbrain doctor --only harness_wiring --json` reports the same state per
5302-harness. opencode and Cursor have no per-turn hook gbrain can install; the
5303-rule reaches them through their instruction file only.

